WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.440 position:58%
But I never shared this with anybody.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.440
OK. But you took it.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.960
That's the problem, OK.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.200
That's where we're at right now.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.920
This is Dr. Shannon You
two hours after she was arrested,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.480 position:59%
and when the FBI picked her up,
they also found a briefcase containing

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.280
$4,000 and suspect
she was about to flee the country.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.600
The then 56-year-old
might make for an unlikely spy,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.200
but nudged by an FBI interrogator,
she's about to talk herself

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.120
into a 14-year prison sentence

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.200
for stealing $120 million
worth of trade secrets.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.240 position:56%
In the process, the case will reveal
details of how industrial espionage

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.840
has become a cornerstone of
China's economic growth.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.880
My name is Jordan Robertson,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:49.880
and I'm a cybersecurity reporter

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.320
for Bloomberg here in London.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.200
This story is about
an incentive system

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.760
that the likes of which the world
has never seen before.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.440 position:59%
was a chemical engineer for Coca-Cola.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.640
She evaluated the coatings
that went inside

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.680 position:58%
all of the cans that Coca-Cola makes.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.640
What these formulations do
is they actually protect

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.200
the can from the Coke.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.760 position:58%
They prevent the chemicals in soda
from eroding the can that they're in.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.240 position:59%
For the companies that make it
like BASF, Dow Chemical and AkzoNobel,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.200
the chemical formulas
are a closely guarded secret.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.800
They cost an estimated
$120 million to develop.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.120 position:59%
So far, no Chinese company has managed
to develop an equivalent,

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.960
and You has the formulas
on her hard drive.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.760
I have never shared any technology
with anybody in China, OK.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:52.480
I go back to China because my mom
is in the last stage of her life,

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:58.000
and so I took every opportunities
to go to China to see my mom.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.600
At the start of the interrogation,

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.920
You is adamant that she's done
nothing wrong,

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.080 position:58%
but she's being a little disingenuous
because she has been going back

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.360
to China to interview
for the Thousand Talents Program.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.040 position:64%
The Thousand Talents Program
is a Chinese national government program,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.920
and it's designed to incentivize

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.920
ethnic Chinese who have moved
abroad to work or study

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.840
to return to China
and to start businesses there.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.840
The critics of the program say it's
really a multibillion-dollar scheme

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.440
that incentivizes them
to steal foreign technology

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.040
and bring it home with them.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.800
And this is the guy that the FBI

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.480
alleges has been helping
her application,

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.760
He's the chief engineer

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.920
for Weihai Jinhong Group.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.800
And that company wants to get into
the business of making BPA-NI,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.640
the chemical lining for Coke cans.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.880 position:98%
Weihai Jinhong did not respond to requests from Bloomberg News for comment.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.360
The interrogation is almost

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.360
a masterclass in how you
unravel a scheme like this,

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.480
because at almost every stage
the FBI catches her in a lie.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.800
The plan was to form a new company.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.240
That's what...

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.720
A joint-venture company?

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.880
Yeah, that's what, that's what
Mr. Liu was thinking, OK.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.320
But it never got there.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.240
For her part,

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.520
You insists that all she ever did
was to introduce the Chinese firm

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.920
to some other companies interested
in getting into the business.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.400
In the interrogation room, this is
where she starts to come unstuck.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.600
Did you guys sign a contract?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.120
For...?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.520
For your work over there?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.920
I did, but there was no work.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.800
There's no work?

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.280
Yeah.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:35.720
Right.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:36.320
There’s no work,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.400 position:59%
because my work, basically,
just introduce, I did not do anything.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.080
Unfortunately for You,
the FBI had a copy of the contract.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.240
Party A Jinhong’s responsibilities
include investing

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.480 position:59%
the initial amount of ¥6 million
($865,000) and providing the location,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.000
among other preparation work,
which is expected to take one year.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.160
This is just talking though.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.600
Ms. You, it's not just talking.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.960
Look, look at the facts.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.080
You signed the contract.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:21.880
Yeah.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.080
They said they would pay you.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.120
The contract was to help

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.400
build a lab. They said when
the lab was built,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.720
you would have
shareholders in that lab.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.160
And then weeks later,

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.960
you were making emails
inquiring about building a lab.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.320
It's not just paper.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.560 position:59%
Then the FBI agents reveal their hand.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.080
They have her voicemails
and have read her text messages.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.240 position:59%
In quick succession, they outline how:
she knew that joining

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.360
the Thousand Talents
might invite the FBI's attention,

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.640
Liu had suggested that she keep her
job at Coca-Cola to, quote,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:01.160 position:56%
You didn't want any publicity around
winning the Thousand Talents

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.720 position:56%
for fear of alerting US authorities.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.480
And the coup de grace?
A voicemail left by her sister.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.720
This time, You’s response
is far more muted.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.520
Well,

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.520
I did not do anything.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.800 position:59%
What her messages reveal about that
defense is she was trying to share it.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.520
She wanted to get paid first,
and ultimately she was prosecuted

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.840
not based on whether she shared it
with the Chinese government or not.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.240
Did she take it?
That was a central question.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.520 position:58%
And her messages show
that the endgame of this was to share

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.680
that information and launch
this company in China and get rich.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.680 position:58%
Yes, this is a tale about
stealing Coke's other secret formula,

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.360
but it's also about how China
is incentivizing espionage far

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.880
beyond the realms of defense
technology and national security

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.600
and into the furthest reaches
of the economy.

